; a joint is the DOF-carrying connector between two links in a kinematic chain
; the link is rigid (no DOF); the joint is where motion happens
; 
; 3D perspective:
; the joint IS a bone's local transform — rotation (revolute) or translation (prismatic)
; its axis is a 3D unit vector in the parent link's local frame
; its value (angle or displacement) IS the DOF state = kona
; in the scene-graph: bone.local = Rot(joint.axis, joint.angle) or Trans(joint.axis, joint.disp)
; 
; physics perspective:
; the joint state IS kona (for revolute) — same quantity, 3D axis specifies which rotation
; angular-velocity = kramanusara of kona wrt time
; torque is applied about the joint axis
; the joint has limits: angle-min, angle-max, speed-max, torque-max
; 
; extraction from text:
; "revolute joint about Z" → joint-type=revolute, joint-axis=[0,0,1]
; "prismatic joint along X" → joint-type=prismatic, joint-axis=[1,0,0]
; "spherical joint" → joint-type=spherical (3 DOF — special case)
; "currently at 0 radians" → joint-angle = 0
; "max speed 2 rad/s" → joint-speed-max = 2
; DOF definition
; state — the actual DOF value
; physical limits
; reference frame structure — this is the key propagation mechanism:
; 
; each joint except the base lives in a chala-apeksha (moving frame) —
; its parent joint's local frame is the reference, and that frame moves.
; the joint itself provides a new chala-apeksha to its child joint.
; the base joint alone has sthira-apeksha (fixed world frame).
; 
; change in joint[i].kona → changes joint[i]'s local frame →
; this IS the chala-apeksha of joint[i+1], joint[i+2], ..., end-effector
; ALL downstream positions, velocities, accelerations are reborn (janya)
; from this changed frame — the phala propagates through the parampara chain
; 
; krama-janya: joint[i]'s transform IS the karana (cause)
; joint[i+1..n] world poses ARE the phala (fruit)
; sambandha:   the transform T[i] is the typed connection — it carries
; position + orientation from frame i to frame i+1

(kosha joint
  (sthita domain-robotics bone chala-apeksha parampara)
  (yukta kinematic-chain scene-graph joint-type joint-axis joint-angle angular-velocity joint-speed-max rated-torque krama-janya sambandha link)
  (abheda kona)
  (phala chala-apeksha))
